    <article>
        <p>I wanted dot paper with cm, inch and 1/4 inch base units, and also wanted markings for sub units.</p>
<p>One <strong>base unit</strong> (1 cm, 1 inch, or quarter inch). On top of that you get 4×, 1×, ½×, and ¼× gray dots, plus a red ⅓× overlay and green every-third 1× dot so you can actually see the 3 vs 4 rhythm without squinting. Dots stay the same physical size when you change base; only the spacing moves. Letter or A4, two pages, no margins, top-left starts on a big 4× dot so lining up a ruler isn’t a guess.</p>
<p><code>./start.sh</code> for one file, <code>./generate-all.sh</code> if you want every combo in <code>output/</code>. README has a cheat sheet for angles if you connect dots on the 1× grid (45°, the 3–4–5 stuff, and “close enough” 30/60).</p>
<p>Repo: <a href="https://github.com/RobKohr/fractional-grid-graph-paper">fractional-grid-graph-paper</a></p>

    </article>
    
